<p>President Trump has publicly urged UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer not to move ahead with a plan to transfer sovereignty of the Chagos Islands to Mauritius, saying the shift could weaken control of Diego Garcia, home to a key U.K.-U.S. military base. Trump tied his warning to rising U.S.-Iran tensions and said the base could matter if Washington needed military options linked to Iran’s nuclear program. Separate reporting says the dispute has intensified because the UK has not granted the United States permission to use Diego Garcia (and other UK-linked bases) for any potential strike on Iran, and that this refusal is tied to Trump’s turn away from supporting the Chagos deal. Beyond the immediate security questions, the row revives a long-running sovereignty and decolonization fight: Britain separated the Chagos Islands from Mauritius in 1965 while Mauritius was still a British colony, and Mauritius says it was forced to give up the territory as a condition of independence.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aD-wSQWTJjlRIoVaz2fYYmSyakxBaYS-CWYBM7OsT61lvkqKDxK8YDRHWG_CzrYemUPFMkTFB2DN4D5PulBvWRKku6owsvRD8-4SY2pxqOrw4FziOaBjbVJ6OAKoBlQge5Dl8VOrg6eXXa29yVCdN6my-njv_qKHJkn7JE4llfUPVzd1BVTDmA5Z5nG9-VQ37-uITkeh9SO1BI8g_0p5_hW2xOQrRewat0pfdHJtzl1D1WNBzngPP4Yj3Q2qVd3mzgqxBxoczVHO' alt='UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer (image used with Firstpost story about Diego Garcia basing permissions).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Bases mentioned: Trump said Diego Garcia and the airfield at Fairford could be needed if Iran ‘decide not to make a deal,’ casting them as important to protecting the UK and other partners.</li><li>UK refusal: The Guardian, NDTV and Firstpost report that the UK has not approved US use of Diego Garcia for a potential Iran strike, and frame that decision as a key source of the current friction.</li><li>Deal mechanics: Trump criticized a proposal described as transferring sovereignty to Mauritius while still allowing the UK and US to keep using the Diego Garcia base.</li><li>Colonial-era split: TIME recounts that Britain separated the Chagos Islands from Mauritius in 1965 and bought them as an overseas territory for about £3 million, a detail central to Mauritius’ claim.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He called Starmer ‘making a big mistake’ and said the UK ‘should not lose control, for any reason, of Diego Garcia,’ tying the issue to Iran-related security risks. (<a href='https://time.com/7379681/trump-starmer-warning-chagos-islands-iran-risk/'>TIME</a>)</li><li>UK government (reported position): UK officials are described as holding back permission for US use of Diego Garcia for a potential strike on Iran. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/uk-denies-us-president-donald-trump-request-to-use-its-key-base-diego-garcia-for-any-iran-strike-report-11103195#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Guardian reporting: The Guardian says Trump’s turn against the Chagos deal came after the UK blocked the use of Diego Garcia for pre-emptive Iran strikes. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/19/donald-trump-turns-against-uk-chagos-islands-plan-iran'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://time.com/7379681/trump-starmer-warning-chagos-islands-iran-risk/'>Trump Again Warns Starmer Not to ‘Lose Control’ of Chagos Islands, Citing Iran Risk</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/19/donald-trump-turns-against-uk-chagos-islands-plan-iran'>Trump changed mind on Chagos deal ‘after UK blocked use of Diego Garcia for Iran strikes’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/uk-denies-us-president-donald-trump-request-to-use-its-key-base-diego-garcia-for-any-iran-strike-report-11103195#publisher=newsstand'>UK Denies Trump&#x27;s Request To Use Its Key Base For Any Iran Strike: Report</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/starmer-blocks-trump-from-using-raf-bases-in-chagos-islands-for-strike-on-iran-amid-tensions-13981795.html'>Starmer blocks Trump from using RAF bases in Chagos Islands for strike on Iran amid tensions</a> - firstpost.com</li></ul>